thank you for joining us i'm john  langler he was killed on a hectic night  here in las vegas  25 year old jorge gomez shot to death by  metro police at the federal courthouse  during a black lives matter protest  today prosecutors decided the officers  involved will  not face charges hector mejia live in  our newsroom with the latest on the case  hector  good afternoon in a 79 page report the  da's office says the actions of the four  officers who fired the deadly gunshots  were not criminal in nature the report  starts with pictures of an earlier  encounter between  jorge gomez and other officers the night  of the black lives matter protest  back on june 1st of last year gomez seen  wearing a  tactical vest and openly carrying two  guns including  an illegal short barreled rifle  according to that report  it also revealed gomez hid behind a  power box at las vegas boulevard and  fremont street when the crowd  was ordered to disperse four officers in  that incident  felt threatened and drew their guns but  did not fire  later that night within one minute after  metro police officer shea mccollonas  was shot in the head in a separate  incident near circus circus  gomez reportedly appeared again in  downtown  this time he approached officers  guarding the federal courthouse  gomez ignored commands one officer fired  low  lethal rounds and gomez then ran  northbound on las vegas boulevard  fell and picked up a gun he dropped  officers responding to the call  at circus circus came across this  disturbance  four of them fired the deadly rounds at  gomez that reported he raised or  pointed his firearm at them and none of  the officers  wore a body camera meanwhile gomez's  family has a lawsuit against the  officers saying  surveillance video shows he did nothing  wrong  all you got is the officer saying that  he raised the weapon  but the video clearly shows that he did  not  so you want us to believe the liars that  are las vegas metropolitan police  department  today we also learned gomez suffered  eight gunshot wounds the report also  says  gomez's father told an investigator that  the black lives matter movement  recruited gomez in oregon  and that they were paying him to protest  today's report is in addition to a  public  fact-finding review which we told you  about back in april  there's a lot of detail in the 79 page  report we uploaded all of those pages on  our website  eight news now dot com reporting from  our newsroom hector mejia  8 news now hector thank you very much
 

